---
import { Code } from "astro:components";

import ComponentPage from "../../../layouts/ComponentPage.astro";
import SpinnerDemo from "../../../components/SpinnerDemo";
import { codeTheme } from "../../../components/code-theme";
import { componentExamples } from "../../../data/snippets";

const { sizeExample, resultExample } = componentExamples.spinner;
---

<ComponentPage slug="spinner">
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    Use it when you cannot predict the layout of what is loading; otherwise prefer a Skeleton.
  </Fragment>

  <SpinnerDemo slot="demo" client:visible />

  <Fragment slot="usage">
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <li>
        <strong>A status with a name.</strong> The spinner is a <code>role="status"</code> element
        with a visually hidden <code>label</code>, "Loading" by default. Say what is loading, such
        as "Loading comments". The drawing is <code>aria-hidden</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reduced motion.</strong> It spins only when the user has not asked for reduced
        motion. Otherwise it shows three static dots, which still read as "in progress"; a frozen
        arc would look broken.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sizes and color.</strong> <code>sm</code> (16px), <code>default</code> (24px) and
        <code>lg</code> (32px). It draws with the current text color, so it follows forced-colors
        mode too.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Inside a button.</strong> Use the Button's <code>loading</code> prop instead; it
        keeps the button focusable and its name.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="examples">
    <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Size and label</h3>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm [&_pre]:p-4">
      <Code code={sizeExample} lang="tsx" theme={codeTheme} />
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Announcing the result</h3>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      A spinner inserted together with its label is not always announced, and its removal never is.
      Mark the loading area with <code>aria-busy</code>, and say when it is done from a
      <code>role="status"</code> region that is already on the page:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm [&_pre]:p-4">
      <Code code={resultExample} lang="tsx" theme={codeTheme} />
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <p slot="install-notes" class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
    It creates <code data-wrap>components/ui/spinner.tsx</code>, the same path as shadcn's Spinner.
    Spinner and Skeleton are separate items, as in shadcn, so each keeps its import path and you
    install only what you use. It needs only your <code>cn()</code> helper; if your
    <code>lib/utils.ts</code> differs from the current shadcn version, the CLI asks before replacing
    it, and answering no is safe.
  </p>
</ComponentPage>
